	"roles": {
		"woodcutter": {"title": "Woodcutter", "work": "forage",
			"intro": ["Mind the axe. It's sharper than it looks. So am I.", "{name}. I fell the trees. The mill turns them into money. Somebody gets the money."],
			"self": ["Forty years in these woods and I've never cut an oak with a face in it. My father did. Once.",
				"You tap a tree before you cut it. Ask it. If it doesn't answer, you're fine. If it does, run."],
			"talk": ["Felled a beech this morning that groaned like an old man. Felt bad. Stacked it anyway.",
				"My axe has had three new heads and four new hafts. Still my grandfather's axe, though.",
				"Pines split clean. Oaks fight you. Maples are just smug about their colour.",
				"Worst part of the job? The walk home with sap in your beard and the wolves humming.",
				"I count rings on every stump. Found one older than the town last spring. Left it standing.",
				"Sawmill wants more timber every season. The forest grows slower than the mill's appetite.",
				"Shout 'timber' if you like. The trees don't care, but the deer appreciate the warning."]},
		"charcoaler": {"title": "Charcoal-burner", "work": "forage",
			"intro": ["Smell that? That's my kiln. Smoulders for a week. So do I, by the end of it.", "{name}. I burn charcoal up in the woods. Black hands, black lungs, warm hearths."],
			"self": ["You sit up with a kiln all night so it doesn't flare. You hear things. Lights between the trees, laughing.",
