			"talk": ["A good burn's slow and quiet. Rush it and you get ash. Same with people.",
				"Stack the wood in a dome, turf over it, light the heart and wait. Seven days. Every time.",
				"My wife says I smell like a chimney. I say she married one.",
				"Rain got into the kiln last week. Lost a whole stack. Sat in the mud and laughed. What else?",
				"Charcoal's lighter than wood and burns hotter. Best trick the forest ever taught us.",
				"Wolves keep clear of my kiln. Smoke in their noses. Lucky for me, unlucky for the deer."]},
		"herbalist": {"title": "Herbalist", "work": "home",
			"intro": ["Cut? Bitten? Cursed? I do the first two. The third costs extra.", "I'm {name}. Roots, bark, the right mushrooms. Never the wrong ones."],
			"self": ["The red ones with the white spots will show you the spirits. They'll also stop your heart. Mostly the second.",
				"My gran said every tree in the deep wood has a name, and it remembers who cut its brothers."],
			"talk": ["Willow bark for the head, yarrow for cuts, valerian for sleep. Cider for everything else.",
				"Three woodcutters came in with splinters today. Same tree. I think it's doing it on purpose.",
				"I dry my herbs in the rafters. The house smells like a meadow and looks like a bird's nest.",
				"Never pick a mushroom you can't name twice. Once for you, once for whoever buries you.",
				"Folk only visit me when they're ill. It's a lonely trade, healing. Sit a while, if you like.",
				"A fox got into my drying shed and ate the sleeping herbs. Snored on my doorstep for two days."]},
		"forager": {"title": "Mushroom-seller", "work": "market",
			"intro": ["Chanterelles, ceps, a basket of hedgehogs. Mushrooms, not the animals.", "{name}. I pick what the woods give. The woods are generous this year. Suspicious, that."],
			"self": ["I found a ring of toadstools last week bigger than the square. Didn't step in it. I'm not daft.",
				"Best picking's at dawn when the mist's down. Worst company, too. Things walk in the mist."],
			"talk": ["Mushrooms are honest. They tell you exactly what they are, if you listen properly.",
				"Sold a whole basket of ceps before noon. The cook bought half. Expect them in the stew.",
				"My knees ache from kneeling in the moss all morning. Worth it, though. Look at these!",
				"There's a patch of truffles I'll never tell a soul about. Not even you. Especially not you.",
				"Deer eat the good ones before I find them. I've started getting up before the deer.",
				"Autumn's my season. The rest of the year I'm just someone with an empty basket and opinions."]},
		"storyteller": {"title": "Storyteller", "work": "plaza",
			"intro": ["A new face! Sit. I'll tell you about the Huntsman. Everyone here's heard it, they won't mind. They'll leave.", "Old {name}. I tell the stories so the young ones keep out of the deep wood."],
			"self": ["When the leaves turn red the old wood wakes. It sleeps through summer and winter, but autumn's its season.",
				"There's a castle in these woods older than the town. The lord there hunted something he shouldn't. It's hunting him back. Still."],
			"talk": ["The young ones laugh at my stories by day. At night they knock on my door for the endings.",
				"A story's like a fire. Feed it slow and everyone stays close. Feed it fast and they scatter.",
				"I've told the tale of the Huntsman four hundred times. It changes a little each time. So does he.",
				"My voice is going. Too many winters shouting over the mill. Lean in, the good bits are quiet.",
				"Pirates make the best listeners. They've done half the things in my stories, and lied about the rest.",
				"Nobody pays a storyteller in coin. They pay in cider and silence. I'll take both."]},
		"raftsman": {"title": "Raftsman", "work": "nets",
			"intro": ["You came by sea? Odd. Everything else here comes down the river.", "{name}. I ride the logs down from the mill to the landing. Mostly on top of them."],
			"self": ["The river's quick past the falls. I've gone over twice. The logs came out fine.",
				"Bargemen don't whistle on the water here. The wisps follow a whistle. Everyone knows that."],
			"talk": ["You steer a raft with your feet, not the pole. The pole's for show, and for wolves.",
