				"Lost a boot to the falls last month. Saw it float past the landing a day later. Waved.",
				"River's in a good mood today. Brown and lazy. When she's green and quick, I stay ashore.",
				"My knees are wet from spring to winter. In winter they're frozen, which is drier.",
				"Otters ride my logs sometimes. I don't charge them. Fellow professionals."]},
		"presser": {"title": "Cider-presser", "work": "market",
			"intro": ["First pressing of the year. Try it. No, the whole cup. That's how you know.", "{name}. Apples from the old orchards, the press by the mill, a barrel for every house."],
			"self": ["Leave a cup on the stump by the orchard gate every autumn. For the folk in the trees. We always have.",
				"A sailor drank three cups of the strong stuff and swore he saw an oak walk. We let him believe it was the cider."],
			"talk": ["Sour apples make the best cider. Sweet ones make the best pies. I make both, badly, joyfully.",
				"Wasps love the press more than I do. I've made peace with them. Mostly.",
				"Every barrel has a name. That one's Old Grumble. Keep away from him, he bites back.",
				"Pressed four hundred apples before breakfast. Arms like a shipwright, sticky to the elbow.",
				"Some years the orchard gives little. This year it's showering us. Something's pleased.",
				"Cider's best in the cold. Drink it here by the fire and you'll know why folk stay."]},
	},
	"barks": {
		"day": ["Turning nicely, the leaves. Pretty, till they're all on your roof.", "Mill's busy today. Hear it? That's money, that sound.", "Smoke from the charcoal kilns again. Wind's from the east.",
			"Keep to the paths in the deep wood. The paths are ours. The rest isn't.", "Good felling weather. Dry, still. The trees won't see it coming.", "Mist's lifting. Should be clear by noon. Should be.",
			"Saw blade's sung all morning. Pine today, by the smell.", "Deer were in the orchard again. Bold as anything.",
			"Maples are going red early this year. Hard winter coming.", "Sawdust in my hair, my tea, my boots. Sawdust in my dreams.",
			"River's calm. The rafts will make good time today.", "Woodpecker's been at my door frame since dawn. Persistent fellow.",
			"A pirate ship in the bay? Hope they're buying timber.", "Acorns everywhere. The squirrels are getting fat and smug.",
			"Squint and you can see the falls from here on a clear day.", "Fresh bread and fresh pine. Smells like a good day.",
			"Heard wolves at first light. Far off, thank goodness.", "Another cartload for the mill. My back's filing a complaint.",
			"Sun through the leaves. Gold everywhere. Can't complain today."],
		"evening": ["Light goes fast under the trees this time of year.", "Inn's warm and the cider's on. Best end to a day there is.", "Sun's down. Bring the logs in, bar the shutters.",
			"Listen. Owls. When the owls stop, that's when to worry.", "Mill's gone quiet. Strange how loud that silence is.",
			"Mist coming off the river. Get home before it thickens.", "Lamps are going on up the hill. Pretty, from here.",
			"Supper's venison stew. Third night running. Not complaining.", "Wolves start up about now. Ignore them. Mostly.",
			"Woodsmoke from every chimney. That's the town saying goodnight.", "Stack the axes inside. Rust loves the evening dew.",
			"Red sky over the maples. Fair weather tomorrow, they say.", "Deer come down to drink at dusk. Stand still and watch.",
			"Cold's settling in. Time for the thick coat and thicker cider.", "Bats over the mill pond. Means the midges are out. Lovely.",
			"Long day. My arms feel like two felled logs.", "Somebody's singing at the inn already. Badly, as usual.",
			"Fog's in the valley. Can't see the river, only hear it.", "Count the children before the gates shut. Twice, to be sure."],
		"night": ["Don't follow the lights in the trees. Whatever they promise you.", "Can't sleep. Something heavy walking past the woodpiles.",
			"Shh. Hear the horn? That's the Hunt. Get indoors.", "Keep your lantern low. Things in the wood notice a bright one.",
			"Wolves are close tonight. Listen. That's not the wind.", "Moon's full. Nobody cuts timber under a full moon here.",
			"Owl on the roof again. Staring. It knows something.", "Mushrooms glowing in the ditch. Never seen so many.",
			"Night watch. Dull, mostly. Mostly is the word to hold onto.", "Antlers clattered on the bark up the hill. Big ones.",
			"Bolt your door. Not for wolves. Wolves don't knock.", "The river sounds different at night. Deeper. Hungrier.",
			"Cold enough to see your breath. Cider keeps the chill off.", "Stars over the pines. Almost worth the shivering.",
			"Fog's thick as wool. Hold the fence and walk slow.", "Who's out at this hour? Oh. A pirate. That's fine, then.",
			"Something laughed by the woodpiles. I'm choosing to think it was a fox.", "Can you hear the mill wheel? It's meant to be stopped.",
			"Late for honest folk. Early for the things in the woods."],
		"nets": ["River's high. Good for the rafts, bad for the nets.", "Pass me that float. The red one. Thank you.", "Trout this morning. Fat ones. The river's kind in autumn.",
			"Knots for nets, knots for rafts. My fingers know no others.", "Pike got through this one. Look at the hole. Rude.",
			"Salmon run's coming. Then nobody sleeps on this pier.", "Eel in the net again. Slippery thief, but he tastes fine."],
		"forage": ["Fresh deer slots. Big stag, by the look.", "Boar's been rooting here. Turned the whole bank over.", "Ceps under this one. Help me pick, or keep walking.",
			"Wolf tracks over the deer tracks. Not a good sign.", "Chestnuts falling. Duck and fill your pockets.",
			"Blackberries, the last of them. Sour, but free.", "Hush. A stag in the clearing. Don't move."],
		"dock": ["Logs go out on the next ship. Mind your feet on the landing.", "Tide's turning. You'll want to be off before dark.", "Your ship? Nice timber in her. Not ours, mind.",
			"Stack the planks by size, or the shipwright shouts.", "Gulls don't come this far up. Too many trees, they think.",
			"Watch the mooring ropes. Slick with moss this time of year.", "Sea's grey today. Ship from the mainland's late again."],
		"boats": ["Every raft here's been down the falls at least once. Every rafter too.", "Hand me that pole. No, the long one.",
			"Lash the logs tight, or the river unlashes them for you.", "This punt leaks. That's why it's cheap. Want it?",
			"Pitch on the seams, moss in the cracks. She'll float.", "River took my hat at the bend. She charges a toll.",
