		"home": ["Woodpile's half done. It's always half done.", "The children are playing by the mill race. I hope.", "If you see a cat with one ear, he's ours. He's lying, whatever he tells you.",
			"Roof needs fresh shingles before the snow. Again.", "Leaves in the gutter, leaves on the step. Leaves in the soup.",
			"Smoke's not drawing. Some bird's nested in my chimney.", "Kindling first, then the logs. My gran's way."],
		"plaza": ["Sit by the fire. It's free, the fire.", "The square oak's older than the town. Older than the island, some say.", "Elder's got a bee in her bonnet. A real one, possibly.",
			"Harvest dance is next week. Practise your stepping.", "Old men by the fire, arguing about rain. Every day.",
			"Somebody carved their name in the oak. The oak won't forget.", "Chestnuts roasting. Ask nicely and you'll get a handful."],
		"inn": ["Pull up a stool. The good seats are for regulars. Become one.", "This round's on the woodcutters. They don't know that yet.", "To the captains! May their sails hold and their timber be ours.",
			"Hot cider with cinnamon. Cures colds, grief and good sense.", "Keep the door shut. The draught off the woods bites.",
			"Bard's late. Probably lost in the mist. Again.", "Woodcutters at that table, raftsmen at this one. Don't mix them."],
		"workshop": ["Measure twice, saw once, curse three times.", "Oak for the frame, pine for the panels, ash for the handles.",
			"Saw's dull. Pass me the file and mind the teeth.", "Making a cradle. Third this season. Long winter last year.",
			"Sawdust is gold to the charcoalers. They take it by the sack.", "This chair's got a wobble. I'll find it. I always do.",
